<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- LoopHoldingGate — PastCast's loading screen: the map band is FROSTED and takes no input while a loop loads.
     Nothing on the map should be readable (the user's call) — only colour washes. Drawn over the map band by
     MainWindow; state is Radar.LoopGate (LoopHoldingGateViewModel).

     FROSTING = two layers, two knobs:
       • the BLUR is in the PAGE (map.js setMapBlur on #panes, LoopHoldingGateViewModel.MapBlurPx = 14) — WinUI's
         in-app acrylic doesn't reliably blur a WebView2 behind it, a CSS filter does, every pane at once;
       • the DIM is here (Root's Background, #C7 = 78% black). The pane notches are WinUI, so they get the dim only.
     Tune the pair together: more blur buys a lighter dim.

       ┌───────────────────────── map band, blurred + dimmed ─────────────────────┐
       │                                                                           │
       │   ╭─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮     │ ← EVENT BAND, AT LEAST 560 (the
       │   │        ≋   Loading May 3, 1999 Bridge Creek-Moore, OK           │     │   bars' width): the type pill's
       │   │              KTLX · Mon May 3, 1999 · 6:00 PM–8:00 PM           │     │   INK on its deep shade; 40 px
       │   ╰─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯     │   picture + words CENTRED as one
       │                              ↕ 22                                         │   group. Title ONE line (a long one
       │        This is raw radar data, not a video. A radar sends a new scan …    │   grows the band, the bars never
       │                              ↕ 28                                         │   move); site line WHITE, centred.
       │                                                                           │ ← WHY (WhyText), 17 pt, WHITE, 400
       │    22 / 28   ▐█▌▐█▌▐█▌▐█▌▐▄▌▐▃▌▐ ▌▐▂▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌      │ ← BARS, layout C+E: two
       │    downloaded 6:35 PM scan · 2.1 of 4.3 MB           12 at once · 61 MB   │   Primitives/LoopLoadProgressBar,
       │                              ↕ 22                                         │   560 wide, a cell per frame
       │    14 / 28   ▐█▌▐█▌▐█▌▐█▌▐█▌▐█▌▐▄▌▐█▌▐▃▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌▐ ▌      │   (grey = download bytes,
       │    built     6:30 PM scan · Decoding                  3 at once · 45%     │   blue = build steps)
       │                              ↕ 100 px                                     │
       │                             [ Cancel load ]                               │
       │                              dark red fill                                │
       └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
       READY (built while the screen was SEEN): "Ready: …" / "Loop ready", bars full, "That took 2 minutes and 14
       seconds to load." under the frames bar (ElapsedText — the same clock the load-time log records), and ONE accent button
       [ View event ] / [ View loop ] in place of the actions — the screen waits for it. A load finishing inside
       FadeInDelayMs never showed the gate, so it just releases.

       ⚠️ NO "Use the map" (removed 2026-10-10, the user's call, with its confirm, the bar's "Loading the loop" line and
          the "don't hold future loads" opt-out): Cancel is the only way off the gate mid-load.
       "Cancel load" → progress + buttons swap for a popup: "Load cancelled" + KeptText + [Got it].

     ⚠️ RequestedTheme="Dark" ON PURPOSE: whatever the app theme, this always sits on a DARKENED map, so its
     text, checkbox and buttons are the dark theme's. Its colours are literals for the same reason — the
     backdrop is fixed, not themed. The built bar's blue matches the scrubber's lit cells in spirit only.
     ⚠️ Fade: hit-testing switches INSTANTLY (the map is gated from the first moment), but the dim AND the blur
     only start after LoopHoldingGateViewModel.FadeInDelayMs, so a cached load that finishes at once never
     flashes the screen.
     ⚠️ Wording lives in the view model (Title, KeptText, the counts) — not here. -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.LoopHoldingGate"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:prim="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <!-- Background = the DIM (78% near-black). Tune with MapBlurPx — see the header. -->
    <Grid x:Name="Root" Background="#C7080A0E" RequestedTheme="Dark" Opacity="0" IsHitTestVisible="False">
        <Grid.OpacityTransition>
            <ScalarTransition Duration="0:0:0.3"/>
        </Grid.OpacityTransition>

        <!-- Bottom margin = ContentBottomInset (the bottom chrome's opaque tiers), so the content centres on the
             VISIBLE map: the gate itself spans the whole window, under the chrome (see MainWindow). -->
        <!-- NO width here: the event band may grow past the bars (its title never wraps). The BARS hold 560 themselves
             (40 frames ≈ 7.6 px a cell; the Radar memory budget can ask for more, cells just narrow); the why line keeps
             its 400 measure. -->
        <StackPanel HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    Margin="{x:Bind BottomInset(ContentBottomInset), Mode=OneWay}">

            <!-- PROGRESS: title, event, the two bars, the counts. -->
            <StackPanel Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsProgressShown, Mode=OneWay}">
                <!-- THE EVENT BAND, above everything (the user's call 2026-10-04): what's loading, in the PastCast type
                     pill's scheme — the type's INK (KindInk) on its deep shade (KindBand), full width so it lines up with
                     the bars (big counts included). Other = your own timeframe or an untyped event → grey + radar rings. -->
                <!-- ⚠️ MinWidth = the bars' 560, centred: a short title leaves room, a long one GROWS the band
                     sideways (the title is one line, never wrapped) — the bars never resize. -->
                <Border Background="{x:Bind KindBand(ViewModel.EventKind), Mode=OneWay}" CornerRadius="8"
                        MinWidth="560" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Padding="16,14" Margin="0,0,0,22">
                    <!-- Picture + words are ONE group, CENTRED in the band at every title length. -->
                    <Grid ColumnSpacing="16" HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <!-- The picture: one single-colour drawing per type, drawn on a 64-unit square, scaled to 40 px;
                             strokes only, round caps. -->
                        <Viewbox Width="40" Height="40" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <Grid Width="64" Height="64">
                                <Path Visibility="{x:Bind KindShown(ViewModel.EventKind, 'Tornado'), Mode=OneWay}"
                                      Stroke="{x:Bind KindInk(ViewModel.EventKind), Mode=OneWay}" StrokeThickness="4.5"
                                      StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round"
                                      Data="M8,12 H56 M13,21 H51 M19,30 H47 M24,39 H43 M28,48 H39 M31,56 H35"/>
                                <Path Visibility="{x:Bind KindShown(ViewModel.EventKind, 'Hurricane'), Mode=OneWay}"
                                      Stroke="{x:Bind KindInk(ViewModel.EventKind), Mode=OneWay}" StrokeThickness="5"
                                      StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round"
                                      Data="M24.5,32 A7.5,7.5 0 1 1 39.5,32 A7.5,7.5 0 1 1 24.5,32 M32,24.5 C30,13 38,7 52,7 M32,39.5 C34,51 26,57 12,57"/>
                                <Path Visibility="{x:Bind KindShown(ViewModel.EventKind, 'Derecho'), Mode=OneWay}"
                                      Stroke="{x:Bind KindInk(ViewModel.EventKind), Mode=OneWay}" StrokeThickness="4.5"
                                      StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round" StrokeLineJoin="Round"
                                      Data="M14,8 Q44,32 14,56 M30,32 H56 M49,25 L56,32 L49,39 M25,18 H44 M25,46 H44"/>
                                <Path Visibility="{x:Bind KindShown(ViewModel.EventKind, 'Other'), Mode=OneWay}"
                                      Stroke="{x:Bind KindInk(ViewModel.EventKind), Mode=OneWay}" StrokeThickness="4"
                                      StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round"
                                      Data="M10,32 A22,22 0 1 1 54,32 A22,22 0 1 1 10,32 M20,32 A12,12 0 1 1 44,32 A12,12 0 1 1 20,32 M32,32 L48,16"/>
                            </Grid>
                        </Viewbox>
                        <!-- ⚠️ TYPE SCALE (the user's call, 2026-10-02; why line 14 → 17 on 2026-10-04): the TITLE is
                             the largest text here (24), the why line next (17), everything else 12–13. -->
                        <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Title, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="24" LineHeight="30"
                                       FontWeight="SemiBold" TextWrapping="NoWrap"
                                       Foreground="{x:Bind KindInk(ViewModel.EventKind), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                            <!-- The site + time line: WHITE, centred under the title. -->
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.EventLine, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="12" Margin="0,4,0,0"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" Foreground="#FFFFFFFF"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Grid>
                </Border>

                <!-- THE WHY LINE (the user's call, 2026-10-02): why a loop takes time. Under the band since 2026-10-04. -->
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Why}" FontSize="17" LineHeight="25" TextWrapping="Wrap" Width="400"
                           TextAlignment="Center" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,0,28" Foreground="#FFFFFFFF"/>

                <!-- THE BARS (layout C+E, the user's call 2026-10-04): Primitives/LoopLoadProgressBar — a big count
                     beside one cell per frame, each filled by how far THAT frame has got (RadarViewModel
                     .RefreshLoopGateCells), the oldest frame in progress named under the cells. Grey = downloads, the
                     scrubber's blue = builds. -->
                <prim:LoopLoadProgressBar Label="downloaded" Fill="#FF9AA4B2" Width="560"
                                          Count="{x:Bind ViewModel.Downloaded, Mode=OneWay}"
                                          Total="{x:Bind ViewModel.Total, Mode=OneWay}"
                                          Cells="{x:Bind ViewModel.DownloadCells, Mode=OneWay}"
                                          Caption="{x:Bind ViewModel.DownloadCaption, Mode=OneWay}"
                                          Detail="{x:Bind ViewModel.DownloadDetail, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                <prim:LoopLoadProgressBar Label="built" Fill="#FF5B8DEF" Width="560" Margin="0,22,0,0"
                                          Count="{x:Bind ViewModel.Built, Mode=OneWay}"
                                          Total="{x:Bind ViewModel.Total, Mode=OneWay}"
                                          Cells="{x:Bind ViewModel.BuildCells, Mode=OneWay}"
                                          Caption="{x:Bind ViewModel.BuildCaption, Mode=OneWay}"
                                          Detail="{x:Bind ViewModel.BuildDetail, Mode=OneWay}"/>

                <!-- THE LOAD'S TIME, Ready only: "That took 2 minutes and 14 seconds to load." — Begin → last frame built
                     (the same clock the load-time log records). -->
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.ElapsedText, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="13" Margin="0,18,0,0"
                           TextAlignment="Center" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Foreground="#FFE8EAED"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsReadyShown, Mode=OneWay}"/>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- The 100 px between the information and the actions (the user's spec). -->
            <Border Height="100" Visibility="{x:Bind SpacerShown(ViewModel.IsActionsShown, ViewModel.IsReadyShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>

            <!-- READY: the loop is built; the screen WAITS for this press (the user's call, 2026-10-02 — someone reading
                 the why line isn't yanked onto the map). "View event" for a chosen event, "View loop" otherwise. -->
            <Button HorizontalAlignment="Center" MinWidth="132" Padding="22,8" CornerRadius="8"
                    Style="{StaticResource AccentButtonStyle}"
                    Content="{x:Bind ViewModel.ReadyButtonText, Mode=OneWay}"
                    Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsReadyShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                    Click="OnViewReadyClick"/>

            <!-- ACTIONS: Cancel (dark red, brighter on hover/press) — the ONLY way off the gate mid-load. ⚠️ "Use the map"
                 (and its confirm) was REMOVED 2026-10-10, the user's call — don't re-add an escape. -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="12" HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsActionsShown, Mode=OneWay}">
                <Button Content="Cancel load" MinWidth="132" Padding="18,8" CornerRadius="8"
                        IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.AreActionsEnabled, Mode=OneWay}"
                        Click="OnCancelClick">
                    <Button.Resources>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonBackground" Color="#FF7A1F1F"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonBackgroundPointerOver" Color="#FFA32D2D"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonBackgroundPressed" Color="#FFC43C3C"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonBackgroundDisabled" Color="#807A1F1F"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonForeground" Color="#FFF6E9E9"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonForegroundPointerOver" Color="#FFFFFFFF"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonForegroundPressed" Color="#FFFFFFFF"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonForegroundDisabled" Color="#99F6E9E9"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonBorderBrush" Color="Transparent"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonBorderBrushPointerOver" Color="Transparent"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonBorderBrushPressed" Color="Transparent"/>
                        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="ButtonBorderBrushDisabled" Color="Transparent"/>
                    </Button.Resources>
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- CANCELLED: what was kept. -->
            <Border Width="310" Padding="16,14" CornerRadius="8" BorderThickness="1"
                    Background="#F214181E" BorderBrush="#40E8EAED"
                    Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.IsCancelledShown, Mode=OneWay}">
                <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                    <TextBlock Text="Load cancelled" FontSize="14" FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#FFE8EAED"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.KeptText, Mode=OneWay}" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               Foreground="#BFE8EAED" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                    <Button Content="Got it" FontSize="12" Padding="14,5" CornerRadius="8" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                            Click="OnGotItClick"/>
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
